// Test: && and || must not evaluate the right side when the left decides.
//
// 03_logical_ops.zy already checks the truth table, and it passed in every
// engine while the tree-walker evaluated both sides regardless — a truth table
// cannot tell short-circuiting from full evaluation, because the answer is the
// same either way. Only an observable effect on the right-hand side can.
efecto() {
    >> "R"
    <~ #1
}

>> "and-false:" (#0 && efecto()) ¶
>> "and-true:" (#1 && efecto()) ¶
>> "or-true:" (#1 || efecto()) ¶
>> "or-false:" (#0 || efecto()) ¶
